[2026-05-24T11:16:54.755Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_463","type":"reasoning","text":"**Considering CI logs management**\n\nI’m thinking about whether adding CI logs to the repository is a good idea. The user suggests a ci-logs directory, so I wonder if they expect a local file rather than a commit. We want a clean working tree, but leaving the logs untracked might not be the best option. The instruction says to preserve them, so maybe committing is the way to go. However, CI logs are often ephemeral and can be large — I should check the .gitignore."}}
